# What never belongs in the image. Everything else is copied, because the server
# reads the HTML shells, the CSVs, the indices and lib/ at runtime and guessing
# wrong there fails at request time on one route rather than at build time.

.git
.gitattributes
.github
node_modules

# The play-by-play file: 388MB, Git LFS, and input to scripts/build-indices.mjs
# rather than to the server. data/indices/ is committed and the server prefers
# it, falling back to the CSVs only if an artifact is missing or stale.
#
# Measured, not assumed: with this file moved aside the server boots, loads all
# 13 artifacts in 3.6s, and serves /, /1982, /records and a box score. It takes
# data/ from 464MB to 76MB — the remaining 76MB is gameinfo, batting, pitching,
# fielding, biofile and teamstats, which stay because they are the fallback the
# server reads if an artifact is ever missing or stale. Dropping those too would
# turn a slow boot into a broken one.
#
# The clone is a separate matter — a build host that smudges LFS still downloads
# it before this file gets a say. See DEPLOYING.md.
data/plays.lfs.csv

# Test suite and its fixtures: 198 tests that run in CI and locally, never in
# the container.
test

# Render-check captures.
.render

# scripts/ is NOT excluded, and the comment that used to say it was build
# tooling was wrong in a way that reached production.
#
# server.js imports ARTIFACT_DIR, FORMAT and reviver from
# scripts/build-indices.mjs to *read* the committed indices. Excluding the
# directory made that import fail, and the failure is caught: the server logged
# "rebuilding from CSV" and carried on. With plays.lfs.csv also excluded — quite
# correctly, it is 388MB — the scoring-plays collector then had nothing to read,
# so every box score rendered without its Scoring Summary while returning 200.
#
# Two exclusions that were each defensible combined into a silent data loss. The
# directory is 28KB.

# Notes for people, not for the runtime.
CLAUDE.md
